1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:01,818
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:05,547
In this lesson, we will build a roster
dispatch can use.

3
00:00:05,758 --> 00:00:09,413
An out-of-date roster leaves dispatchers
guessing which station,

4
00:00:09,684 --> 00:00:12,140
team, or role a member belongs to.

5
00:00:12,299 --> 00:00:16,013
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,013 --> 00:00:18,135
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,945 --> 00:00:23,913
A volunteer department creates Station 1
and Station 2 groups, invites

8
00:00:23,916 --> 00:00:27,594
24 members and assigns Engineer and
Firefighter roles.

9
00:00:27,827 --> 00:00:32,848
Dispatch, notifications, permissions and
reports all start from who belongs

10
00:00:32,848 --> 00:00:35,582
to which group, so set this up first.

11
00:00:35,729 --> 00:00:39,701
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:39,701 --> 00:00:42,147
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:42,957 --> 00:00:47,263
Personnel. Member accounts, contact
details and status.

14
00:00:47,451 --> 00:00:51,011
Invite members or add them directly, then
check that each has

15
00:00:51,013 --> 00:00:53,148
a mobile number or email address.

16
00:00:53,949 --> 00:00:55,078
Manage Invites.

17
00:00:55,285 --> 00:00:58,681
Email invitations for new members to join
the department.

18
00:00:58,913 --> 00:01:02,801
Send invitations and follow up on any that
have not been accepted.

19
00:01:03,571 --> 00:01:04,878
Groups & Stations.

20
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:08,187
Stations and groups that organize members
and units.

21
00:01:08,396 --> 00:01:13,140
Create a station group for each station
with its address, and organizational

22
00:01:13,143 --> 00:01:15,551
groups for teams, then add members.

23
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:17,443
Personnel roles.

24
00:01:17,652 --> 00:01:20,906
Roles such as Firefighter, EMT or Officer.

25
00:01:21,089 --> 00:01:25,338
Create the roles you dispatch or report
on, and assign them to members.

26
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:26,973
Add Person.

27
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:31,032
Create a member account directly instead
of sending an invitation.

28
00:01:31,265 --> 00:01:35,510
Have your member list with email addresses
or mobile numbers, and decide

29
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,577
how stations or teams are grouped.

30
00:01:38,381 --> 00:01:39,090
New Group.

31
00:01:39,329 --> 00:01:41,009
Create a station or group.

32
00:01:41,265 --> 00:01:45,513
Have your member list with email addresses
or mobile numbers, and decide

33
00:01:45,514 --> 00:01:47,571
how stations or teams are grouped.

34
00:01:48,407 --> 00:01:53,786
For the training scenario, work in this
order. Step 1. Create Station 1

35
00:01:53,786 --> 00:01:55,840
and Station 2 with their addresses.

36
00:01:56,099 --> 00:02:00,345
Step 2. Invite sample members and assign
their station groups.

37
00:02:00,598 --> 00:02:05,253
Step 3. Create Engineer and Officer roles
and assign them deliberately.

38
00:02:06,047 --> 00:02:07,697
Now verify the result.

39
00:02:07,906 --> 00:02:11,540
Verify a sample member appears in the
correct group and role.

40
00:02:11,732 --> 00:02:15,410
Check an accepted invitation and the
member contact details.

41
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:20,455
A common problem to watch for: An
invitation is not an accepted membership.

42
00:02:20,656 --> 00:02:23,830
A role label is not proof of a current
certification.

43
00:02:24,022 --> 00:02:25,490
Review both separately.

44
00:02:26,248 --> 00:02:28,090
Your practice task is simple.

45
00:02:28,244 --> 00:02:33,574
Invite one sample member, assign a station
and role, and have that member sign in.

46
00:02:33,793 --> 00:02:35,844
Track unaccepted invitations.

47
00:02:36,043 --> 00:02:40,554
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

48
00:02:40,696 --> 00:02:44,659
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

